# .NET Core and Visual Studio temporary files, binaries, and packages.

## Ignore all build output folders
# This is the most important rule. It ignores the entire 'bin' and 'obj' folders
# where all binaries (.dll, .exe) and intermediate files are created.
[Bb]in/
[Oo]bj/

## IDE and user-specific files
# These files store your personal IDE settings, open tabs, window layouts, etc.
# They should never be shared in source control.
.vs/
*.suo
*.user
*.csproj.user

## Secrets and environment configuration
# launchSettings.json often contains environment variables for local debugging.
# While not always a secret, it's good practice to ignore it to avoid conflicts.
# IMPORTANT: NEVER commit appsettings.json files with real passwords or API keys.
Properties/launchSettings.json

## Build results
[Rr]elease/
[Dd]ebug/
[Tt]est[Rr]esult*/
[Bb]uild[Ll]og.*
*.[Pp]ublish.xml
*.nupkg
*.snk

## Log files
# Ignore any log files generated by the application.
*.log
logs/

## Other
# OS-generated files
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Rider / ReSharper specific files
.idea/
*.sln.DotSettings.user
